  m_Name: 1960 pigeons
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  title: Feeding Pigeons Prohibited 1960s
  info: Feeding pigeons is illegal to control the pigeon population and prevent hygiene
    issues, as large flocks of pigeons contribute to the spread of diseases like
    psittacosis. The law is enforced in parks, streets, and public spaces to deter
    such behavior. First-time offenders face a fine of up to SGD 500, while repeat
    violations can lead to heavier penalties. Public education campaigns emphasize
    the ecological and health risks of overfeeding urban wildlife.
  image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: cce8898b6e8aa4da6bb90f5e956f42e7, type: 3}
